  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Lengthy run of dry and mild weather continues \ninto early November before coming to an end by late next week \n\nAnother very pleasant and comfortable weekend to close out \nOctober (Halloween) and start November (ending daylight saving \ntime). \n\nThe latest model guidance continues to grow in agreement with \nthe progression of a CONUS-crossing upper trough eventually \nreaching the eastern U.S. by the second half of next week.\nHighest odds for rain are currently placed around Thursday \n11/5. There also continues to be some indications that rich \nGulf moisture will be pulled northward along a well defined \nnorth south oriented frontal zone accompanying the full \nlatitude upper trough which could result in moderate to heavy \nrainfall.",
